Z||000000||SloPonti||04-30-2000||02:02 AM||||well today i got a four wheel alignment done today and the car drives perfectly straight now!! but at 40mph i get a noise-kinda like a humming of the tires and it gets worse as you speed to 50 and then it goes away after that but then comes back at about 55 to 60! this is wierd! it is very loud and annoying! some thing about the car now! <BR>84 fiero<BR>new four cylinder<BR>all new tires front and rear<BR>all new suspension front and rear<BR>new cv joints!<BR>new brakes<P>and everything was fine untill i got the alignment today and now this humming noise! does anyone else have this?<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||13
Z||000001||Ozzy||04-30-2000||04:34 AM||||I have a noise that recently developed in the rear of my 88 coupe Sloponti. It sounds like big tread tires on a 4wd truck! (Almost) It is a bit more constant than you describe though. Starts around 20 mph and rises in pitch proportionate to vehicle speed. I have 2 thoughts. First occured to me and was sugested in the relevant thread I started...wheel bearings, and the second which I did not think of was rear toe in/out. <P>I have not had time to investigate it further but being as you just had a rear alignment too, maybe that is it. Perhaps they screwed something up?<P>I put the Coupe on jackstands and ran the rear end and could not hear the noise at all but wheel bearing would not necessarily make noise unless under vertical load. <P>Ozzy||||reg||1
